#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Zero-noise extrapolation with gate folding and custom extrapolation for the "
"latest version of Qiskit mitigation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation with gate folding and custom extrapolation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/gate-"
"folding-with-custom-extrapolation.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) is a technique for mitigating quantum noise "
"in observable expectation value calculations. It works by executing a "
"quantum circuit at increasing noise scales, taking expectation values with "
"respect to those noise scales, and extrapolating to estimate a zero-noise "
"expectation value. Both the noise amplification and extrapolation stages can"
" be implemented in different ways. This guide amplifies the noise with "
"\"digital gate folding\", which means that two-qubit gates are replaced with"
" equivalent sequences of the gate and its inverse. For example, replacing a "
"unitary $U$ with $U U^† U$ would yield a noise amplification factor of 3. "
"You can also implement amplification with probabilistic error amplification "
"(PEA), which needs an additional step of learning a noise model and is "
"covered in the [probabilistic error amplification](/addons/qiskit-"
"mitigation/guides/pea-with-noise-learning) guide. This guide extrapolates "
"using a couple of built-in fitting strategies (linear and exponential), and "
"it also demonstrates how to implement your own custom fitting function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Keep in mind, while ZNE can be effective at mitigating quantum noise for a "
"lower sampling cost than other methods, it comes with no bounds on the "
"bias.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Gate folding](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"mitigation/zne_gate_folding.svg)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The workflow is as follows:\n"
"1. Specify a circuit and observable\n"
"2. Compute exact expectation values using Qiskit's statevector simulator\n"
"3. Compute noisy, unmitigated expectation values\n"
"4. Prepare a ZNE program with digital gate folding and sample circuits of varying noise scales\n"
"5. Extrapolate to the zero-noise limit with built-in and custom fitting functions\n"
"6. Compare the mitigated expectation values\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Specify a circuit and observable {#specify-a-circuit-and-observable}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the site-averaged magnetization $\\langle Z \\rangle_{\\text{avg}}"
" = \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle Z_i \\rangle$ of a Trotterized "
"transverse-field Ising model (TFIM) on eight qubits in a ring topology. You "
"will sweep several values of the strength of the transverse field and plot "
"the magnetization as a function of the field strength.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"mitigation/guides/gate-folding-with-custom-extrapolation/extracted-"
"outputs/f1b76ce7-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute exact expectation values using Qiskit's statevector simulator "
"{#compute-exact-expectation-values-using-qiskits-statevector-simulator}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use Qiskit's ``Statevector`` class to compute the exact expectation value of"
" $Z_i$ on each site for every value of $\\theta$.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
